kers) Collaborate closely with space engineers and scientists to translate mission-related requirements into scalable, robust software solutions Share responsibility for the backend architecture across both tech stacks, with a focus on performance, fault tolerance, and maintainability Plan and document implementation steps, from system architecture through deployment in a cloud-native environment Ensure code quality, automated testing, and adherence to security and development standards Advance CI/CD pipelines, observability, and automation to support stable, continuous releases Analyze and resolve complex issues in distributed systems with a focus on efficiency and reliability Work within small, interdisciplinary teams, contributing your backend expertise to cross-functional projects Your profile Must-haves Degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field, or completed vocational training as a Fachinformatiker (IT specialist) At least 2 years of professional experience with Python for backend development, scripting, automation, or data processing At least 2 years of professional experience in backend software development with Java (Spring Boot or comparable) Solid understanding of microservice architectures, asynchronous systems, and distributed communication patterns Practical experience with testing and code quality assurance Experience with, or willingness to quickly get up to speed on, message-based communication between services (e.g., RabbitMQ or comparable message brokers) and containerization (Docker) Ability to independently plan, implement, and review complex features in close collaboration with engineers and scientists Proactive communication, structured way of working, and good written and spoken English Nice-to-haves Experience with orchestration, particularly Kubernetes Experience with code reviews and adherence to coding standards Solid understanding of software architecture principles, including modular structure, scalability, and maintainability Experience with secure software development Background in or interest in the space or aerospace sector Why us? Flat hierarchy, small teams, flexible working hours Onboarding in Braunschweig, followed by on-site work in Munich Up to 30 days’ vacation & up to 30 days’ workation per year Early responsibility, influence on the technical direction Training budget for your personal development Career paths to support and promote your long-term development Corporate benefits (brand discounts, travel discounts, concert tickets, etc.) Free German language course Bahncard (25 within Braunschweig, 50 outside) Bike leasing Company pension scheme Subsidy towards Hansefit / Wellpass membership Participation in space events and conferences to promote sustainable space travel Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
