    schema:datePosted "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Intro Do you love traveling and are you ready for new challenges in an ambitious, fast-growing and committed company? Then you've come to the right place! Start your career with us as: Backend Engineer (m/f/x) Your responsibilities Travelcircus is seeking an experienced (4+ years) Backend Engineer (m/f/x) to join the development team. We're looking for someone who's passionate about building robust & scalable technology platforms, systems and APIs. You'll be an integral part of the engineering team and will work closely with others throughout our company to deliver the best possible product to our customers. Ideal candidates will have experience with PHP, AI supported software engineering, API development and Service-Oriented Architectures. Things you will work on Building and extending our Platform Services and Booking Systems Designing, developing, and maintaining a robust transactional API platform, that will be used internally and directly by 3rd parties Keeping up with the state-of-the-art of AI assisted development and applying it to everyday tasks Participating in code reviews and pair programming Improving our existing platform codebase which is used by tens of thousands of users on a daily basis Addressing bugs and performance issues What we offer FLEXIBLE WORKING HOURS thanks to part-time and flexitime models as well as remote work (2 days a week) ATTRACTIVE WORK ENVIRONMENT close to Alexanderplatz in a stylish loft office with start-up flair, cooking together, fun & cohesion in a varied working environment and regular team events TRANSPARENT COMMUNICATION thanks to flat hierarchies, fixed feedback cycles and weekly company and team meetings OPTIMAL CAREER OPPORTUNITIES thanks to a comprehensive onboarding program and individual induction, continuous on-the-job training, optimal promotion and further development opportunities ADDITIONAL COMPENSATION & DISCOUNT on the BVG company ticket (local public transport) and discounts with over 800 other providers PERSONAL TRAVEL BUDGET of €1080 per year to spend freely on our entire product portfolio WORK LIFE BALANCE with 28 vacation days, increasing per year of service, with up to 35 days of vacation entitlement as well as company health management and a pension plan Your profile Experience in building web applications and distributed web services (4+ years) Knowledge of PHP / OOP, relational databases and data modelling Good understanding of SQL and the ability to write and debug queries Experience with common AI agents like Claude or Codex; Knowledge of current AI tools, best practices, knowing what is hype and what is useful Experience with Linux/macOS command line Experience using message queues and Elasticsearch is a plus Strong visual, verbal and written communication skills, fluency in english, german is a plus Experience working in Agile environments Do you still have questions or do you want to apply immediately? If you want to develop yourself further and take on responsibility, then you've come to the right place. Please send us your application, including your salary expectations and your earliest possible start date, exclusively via our online application system. Our Team Lead People & Operations will be happy to answer any questions you may have: Ines Krawczyk Team Travelcircus Over the past few years, Travelcircus has developed into an international company with over 100 highly motivated and committed employees who form the basis of our success. If you would like to get to know our team, then take a look at our Instagram Career page - there you will get a first impression of your future colleagues. We expressly declare that we welcome everyone, regardless of gender, nationality or ethnic origin, religion or ideology, disability, age or sexual identity. We look forward to meeting you! Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
