    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-25T06:56:47+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-25T10:39:01+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "interim-fpa-director-6-months-ftc-238082" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "<div class=\"content-intro\"><p>Every mind is unique. Yet much of the world is still built for what’s considered \"normal,\" leaving too many people behind. At Everway, we change that by creating technology that helps everyone understand and be understood. By understanding and addressing the unique needs of each individual, we're creating a world where differences are recognized and valued.</p> <p>Our careers fit real life. When you join us, you’re not just taking a job. You’re joining a movement to build a more neuroinclusive world. We’re a global community of over 800 employees spanning North America, UK, Europe, Australia, and New Zealand. A career here is purposeful and fast-moving, with clear expectations, modern tools, and the clarity to focus on what matters most.&nbsp;</p> <p>Our people are supported and encouraged to show up as they are, with different ways of thinking welcomed and valued. We pride ourselves on our core values that are embedded within our culture. These are to <strong>be curious, have courage, and commit fully</strong>.</p> <p>Join us at Everway - together, we can unlock the full potential of every mind.</p></div><p><strong>About the role</strong></p> <p>The Interim FP&amp;A Director will provide senior support across corporate planning and executive reporting during a critical period for the Finance function. You'll work closely with the SVP, Strategic Finance and VP, Corporate FP&amp;A, with a particular focus on Board reporting, strategic analysis and the company's three-year plan.</p> <p>This is a hands-on interim assignment combining detailed financial modelling and planning with senior stakeholder communication. You'll help translate business performance and forecasts into a clear, credible narrative and maintain the quality and continuity of key Strategic Finance deliverables.</p> <p><em><strong>This is a six-month fixed-term contract role.</strong></em></p> <h2><strong>Main responsibilities</strong></h2> <p>In this role, you will:</p> <ul> <li>Own the preparation and coordination of Board and executive reporting materials, including financial analysis, commentary and final review, ensuring key messages, risks and actions are clear.</li> <li>Support the development of the company's three-year plan, including the narrative connecting strategic priorities with financial outcomes.</li> <li>Build and refine scenario analysis, sensitivities and planning assumptions across revenue, costs, headcount and cash flow.</li> <li>Partner with Finance and business leaders to align assumptions and strengthen the overall planning process.</li> <li>Provide senior day-to-day support to the SVP Strategic Finance, working with the VP of Corporate FP&amp;A and other Strategic Finance VPs across planning, reporting and ad hoc strategic analysis as required.</li> <li>Identify practical improvements to reporting cadence, KPI definition, forecasting discipline and FP&amp;A processes.</li> </ul> <h2><strong>Essential criteria</strong></h2> <ul> <li>3–5+ years of relevant professional experience at a similar level across corporate finance, strategic finance, strategy or management consulting, or FP&amp;A.</li> <li>Experience producing Board packs, executive presentations and decision-support materials for senior stakeholders.</li> <li>Experience supporting long-range planning, budgeting, forecasting and strategic financial modelling.</li> <li>Advanced Excel and financial modelling capability, with experience producing accurate, high-quality planning and reporting outputs.</li> <li>Experience working closely with CFO-level or other senior stakeholders and constructively challenging assumptions.</li> </ul> <h2><strong>Desirable criteria</strong></h2> <ul> <li>Experience in SaaS, technology, PE-backed or similarly dynamic business environments.</li> <li>Experience integrating AI into finance or FP&amp;A working practices.</li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Please submit your application by <strong>Monday 7th September 2026.</strong></p> <p>Please note: applications may close early due to high demand, so early submission is encouraged.</p><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p>Join our team and enjoy a competitive salary with bonus opportunities, flexible work schedules, and comprehensive health and wellness benefits. We offer flexible time off plans, career growth through development programs, and a collaborative, innovative culture where your ideas matter.&nbsp; Ready to make an impact? Apply today and be part of a company that invests in your success!</p> <p>We are committed to providing a Drug-Free Workplace for all employees.</p> <p>We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law.</p> <p>You can view our Recruitment and Selection Policy <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yDxHyVbhh8MK9NnCYdnEAfVSO4rhPCovVbKK8ecxT4U/edit?usp=sharing\">here.</a></p> <p>Please click the link for our <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uAKvHVSRsqZ83CGhM3_3Dc6RPsXwlTdmwdUH7msHkVM/edit?usp=sharing\">Privacy Notice</a></p> <p>&nbsp;</p></div> Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-everway ;
    schema:identifier "arbeitnow-interim-fpa-director-6-months-ftc-238082" ;
    schema:title "Interim FP&A Director (6 Months FTC)" ;
    schema:url <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/everway/interim-fpa-director-6-months-ftc-238082> .

<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-interim-project-senior-devops-consultant-berlin-hq-173895> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-25T10:39:01+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/climate/interim-project-senior-devops-consultant-berlin-hq-173895> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "567c47590050d7be4b3f0e037ae417dce934c469e7f3c261a306e6628d77069d" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-25T06:56:47+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-25T10:39:01+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "interim-project-senior-devops-consultant-berlin-hq-173895" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Job description We are seeking an experienced Senior DevOps Consultant to support a defined project at our Headquarters in Berlin. The assignment is focused on the set-up and further development of our data management and infrastructure platform. The initial consulting engagement is planned for six months, with the possibility of extending the assignment for a further period, potentially up to 12 months in total, subject to project requirements and mutual agreement. The consultant will provide specialist DevOps and data-platform expertise within the scope of the project. The assignment is structured as an independent consulting engagement, with responsibility for delivering agreed project outcomes and technical solutions. The project supports our Climate Policy Team, which is engaged in various projects on climate change mitigation, in particular on energy system transformation, evaluation of emissions scenarios, the 1.5°C global warming limit and evaluation of national climate action. This includes flagship projects such as the Climate Action Tracker and the National Pathways Explorer, for which data is processed and analysed in-house and then published on the respective project websites. As part of the assignment, the consultant will work on the shared data platform and infrastructure used across the organisation. Our platform is self-hosted on our own hardware and currently runs PostgreSQL, MinIO, GitLab CI/CD and containerised workloads on Linux. The consultant is expected to organise and perform the assignment independently, within the agreed project scope and in coordination with relevant project stakeholders. Your responsibilities Build and operate the data platform for advanced analytics and climate modelling, spanning DevOps and data engineering work. Take the platform from single-server deployments to properly separated environments, with orchestration and infrastructure as code. Establish and improve the platform's operational practices, including monitoring, alerting, incident response, capacity planning and performance optimisation. Design and implement the access, identity and secrets model across platform and shared infrastructure. Contribute to the standardisation of production data workflows and platform standards across the organisation. Document what you build (runbooks, architecture notes and handover material) to ensure continuity. Provide technical guidance to data analysts and scientists and support the adoption of good practice in DataOps, security and governance. Evaluate new tools and technologies, run proof-of-concepts, and help define the technical roadmap for our infrastructure. Your profile Relevant Tech Skills Required: Python and shell scripting. Linux servers in production. Container orchestration you have operated yourself, including cluster setup and upgrades (Kubernetes, Docker). Infrastructure as Code and configuration management (Ansible, or equivalent). Operational experience with PostgreSQL (backup and point-in-time recovery, tested restores, version upgrades and connection pooling). Monitoring tools (like Prometheus, Grafana) and alert design. A solid understanding of distributed systems in an on-premise context. Nice to have: S3-compatible object storage operations (MinIO, Ceph). Identity and directory services like LDAP, Keycloak, or SSO integration across self-hosted tools. Virtualisation platforms (Proxmox, KVM). Have actively applied data governance principles to manage data quality, security, and compliance, and understand how to implement controls that protect sensitive information. Some experience deploying AI projects. Qualifications You will ideally have the following qualifications and skills: You have more than 5 years of experience operating Linux servers in production, including on-premise or bare-metal environments (not exclusively managed cloud). Proven ability to build automated pipelines that streamline development, testing and deployment for data-related projects. You are an excellent troubleshooter who excels at diagnosing and fixing data infrastructure and identifying performance bottlenecks. A strong communicator who can collaborate effectively with colleagues and stakeholders in a diverse, interdisciplinary and international environment. Passionate about working at the intersection of Climate Science and Data Engineering (tell us about relevant projects you’ve worked on!). Organised, detail-oriented, and motivated self-starter with strong analytical skills. Proven ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with project stakeholders. Good communication skills in English. Our offer Conditions Application Deadline: The position remains open until filledExpected start of assignment: As soon as possible, by mutual agreement.Location: We would prefer the consultant to be based in Berlin to facilitate effective project coordination, technical collaboration and onboarding, particularly during the initial phase of the assignmentTerms: We are looking for a senior consultant for 6 months with the possibility of extension to up to 12 months in total, subject to project requirements, funding and mutual agreement. Please apply with your CV and cover letter in PDF format exclusively using the application form at the earliest opportunity. Please indicate in your cover letter your earliest possible start date and your expected daily rate. Applications by email or by post can unfortunately not be processed. We encourage you to apply using the application form. We are a diverse and inclusive team and welcome your application regardless of your gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, religion, ethnicity, age, neurodiversity, disability status, citizenship, or any other aspect that makes you unique. Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Experienced, Freelance, Full time" ;
