    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "pharmacy-dispenser-winnersh-88720" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "What is the job? In our pharmacy, every day is about combining pace with precision, always keeping patients at the heart of everything we do. We work in a fast-moving, agile environment where accuracy is paramount, flexibility is essential, and no two days are the same. You will be part of a dedicated team that thrives under pressure, adapts quickly, and takes pride in making a genuine difference to patients’ lives Working as a Pharmacy dispenser supporting the supply of CMBP in a specialist Private pharmacy. This is a niche role in a growing area. The successful candidate will be working alongside specialist Clinical Pharmacists to make CMBP more accessible for all patients. What will you be doing? Receiving and validating prescriptions ready for a clinical check. Processing patient information appropriately. Supporting the Responsible Pharmacist & Technicians in the daily operations of the Pharmacist. Being the first point of contact for any queries to the Pharmacy. Maintaining relevant records for the supply of CMBP. Maintaining stock and security of any CMBP on site. Maintaining communication of prescription to the Department of Health to meet Regulatory Requirements. Supporting governance in the Pharmacy to ensure the pharmacy is operating as safely as possible. What do you need? A UK qualified Pharmacy dispenser Ideally Undertaken CPD-accredited medical cannabis educational programme. Through this will be provided for the successful candidate Self-motivated individual with high levels of attention to detail, able to work accurately, identifying errors quickly and easily Experience in working in the pharmacy dispensary either primary and/or secondary environment Has attention to detail, patience and the ability to remain calm during stressful situations Excellence in communication skills with staff, patients and other healthcare professionals. Professional, ethical and committed to providing excellent customer care Excellent computer literacy with good working knowledge of office applications including Word, Excel and PowerPoint What we offer: Generous Leave: 25 days holiday (rising to 27 after year one and 30 after year three) + 8 bank holidays Pension Matching: Up to 5% employer matching contributions Flexibility and Wellness: Work-from-home options, cycle-to-work scheme, private healthcare and more Growth Opportunities: Collaborate across teams and represent Montu at events, with support to grow your skills and impact Enhanced Maternity & Paternity Leave About Us Montu UK is a leading digital health company specialising in cannabis-based medicines (CBPM), dedicated to improving patient access to safe and effective treatments. Our mission is to transform lives by combining innovative technology with high-quality clinical care, ensuring patients receive the support they need at every step of their journey. As a fast-growing organisation, we offer a collaborative and supportive environment where talented people can develop their careers while contributing to meaningful change in healthcare. At Montu UK, your work has a direct impact on improving patients’ lives and expanding access to modern medical treatments. Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
