    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "remote-cloud-consultant-architect-dusseldorf-96894" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Are you ready to put your expertise to work and transform traditional infrastructures into modern, agile cloud environments? As a Cloud Consultant/Architect with us, you’ll have the opportunity to collaborate with leading organizations and leverage cutting-edge technologies to optimize their data centers. This is your chance: At ITQ, we offer you an environment where you can learn and grow—together with colleagues who maintain high standards of quality. We are passionate about our customers, but equally passionate about developing our people with new skills and ways of working. Your Role at ITQ: As a Cloud Consultant/Architect, you will support our clients in transforming their traditional data centers into modern, flexible, and efficient software-defined environments. Working closely with customers, you’ll understand their business requirements and develop tailored solutions using the latest technologies. You’ll be there to save the day—by simplifying complex data center infrastructures or cloud environments, reducing costs, and increasing overall performance. The Benefits at ITQ: Integration: A comprehensive onboarding process, followed by an informal lunch or dinner with your “buddy.” ITQ: A friendly atmosphere with a strong corporate culture. Regular team events (team building, after-work events, partner/publisher conferences). Flexible working hours and the option for remote work. Excellence: Collaboration with top experts in their field, participation in regular trade fairs and events, as well as global networking opportunities. Involvement in innovative and large-scale projects. Continuous training programs and sponsored certifications. A clear and ambitious vision for the future, with openness to your ideas and feedback. What We Offer You: Numerous opportunities for your personal and professional development. A competitive salary package, a collective bonus, and an annual budget for training and certifications. A company car or mobility budget. A remote work budget to set up your workspace. Social benefits such as retirement provisions and an employee savings plan. The chance to be part of a warm and inclusive team—the ITQ family. Your Tasks and Technologies: You bring solid experience in one or more of the following areas: VMware technologies (one or more) such as VMware vSphere, vSAN, Aria Operations, or NSX; experience in a Dell VxRail environment is a strong plus. Design, implementation, and optimization of AWS architectures, including cloud migrations, security, and cost optimization. Planning, implementation, and administration of Red Hat Enterprise Linux, as well as related technologies such as OpenShift, Ansible, and Satellite. HashiCorp technologies, particularly Terraform for Infrastructure-as-Code and Vault for secret management. You are hands-on experienced with Hyper-Converged Infrastructure (HCI) solutions—experience in this area is an advantage. You have architectural knowledge in the field of SDDC with a solid understanding of x86 virtualization, operating systems, advanced networking, and storage architectures. You hold up-to-date industry-standard certifications and are willing to acquire further certifications. What We Expect From You: You are passionate about your work as a Consultant or Architect and can identify customer use cases and translate them into concrete solutions. You are fluent in German and can communicate confidently in English. You are curious about new technologies—because that’s exactly your thing. You live in Germany. Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "fulltime permanent, Mid" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-itq ;
