    schema:description "Why VMRay At VMRay, you will have the opportunity to shape and develop innovative tools that support our cutting-edge malware analysis and threat detection technologies. As part of our highly collaborative Labs` Tool and Automation team, you will work alongside passionate experts, contribute to maintaining the stability and quality of our software releases and help drive continuous improvements across our development and infrastructure landscape. If you are an experienced Full-Stack Software Engineer (M/F/D) with a passion for building new solutions and an interest in system administration, VMRay offers a dynamic environment where your ideas and expertise can make a real impact. Your Responsibilities Take over responsibility for tools, projects and product components Develop new tools, while taking care of fulfilling the requirements and discuss missing information with the stakeholders Administrate machines and take care of a steady availability of the services in the VMRay Labs' Tools and Automation team, including Amazon AWS hosted components Our Requirements 5+ years of Python development experience Good experiences in some common Python frameworks (e.g. Pika, Boto3, SQLAlchemy, Django, FastAPI) Knowledge of how to work with Code quality in mind (pep8, linters) Knowledge in Test-driven development (Pytest) Experience with REST APIs; Developing server applications (Micro Services), as well as clients Experience with Ansible, PostgreSQL and Jenkins or Bamboo (CI/CD) Experience with common Amazon AWS components and their administration, as well as Kubernetes Experience with RabbitMQ is beneficial Being a fast learner and excellent team player Excellent problem-solving and troubleshooting skills Location Germany, Bochum or Remote (Europe) Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Experienced, Full time, Permanent" ;
