    schema:title "Senior Customer Success Manager (f/m/x)" ;
    schema:url <https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/sparetech/senior-customer-success-manager-430541> .

<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-senior-customer-support-engineer-london-163343> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-25T10:39:01+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/fyxer/senior-customer-support-engineer-london-163343> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "a43f560d4f4f6bd01be23db9f85826fa25058b92e6947679130b69b46cfa6419" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-25T03:04:02+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-25T10:39:01+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "senior-customer-support-engineer-london-163343" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "About Fyxer Since launching in May 2024 we've grown to $30 million in ARR. Fyxer is building an AI executive assistant that handles emails, scheduling and follow-up, freeing people in client-facing roles to focus on their customers. What You'll Be Doing Own the hardest technical tickets in the business end to end, including the customer conversation, from first report through to resolution Dogfood Fyxer’s own products, give feedback, and influence our roadmap Establish blast radius before escalating, because one customer reporting something is a ticket and forty-seven accounts in the same broken state is an incident Call bug, incident or user error correctly and quickly, and declare it when it's an incident Write escalations Engineering can act on without a single follow-up question, and stay on them until they land Spot patterns across Linear and the queue, raising a tracker before the fifth report of something becomes the tenth Reduce the need for your own role through runbooks, saved queries, Parahelp knowledge, and hands-on upskilling of our senior agents Here's the honest version of why this role exists. In one recent three-month window we escalated 47 tickets to Engineering and two of them were resolved. Engineering is capacity-constrained, and a third of what we sent them was correctly deprioritised. So this isn't a role that escalates better, it's one that resolves. You'll be backed by strong Customer Success and Product Engineering teams, and given read-only access to our codebase through Cursor, to our data through our internal tooling, and to our production logs to do it. What Success Looks Like You resolve a growing share of technical escalations without Engineering ever being involved Your escalations are complete, so Engineer can act on them quickly You use AI and you catch it when it's wrong, before it reaches a customer You hold a customer's confidence while you investigate, rather than handing them back to someone else Our senior agents are visibly more capable six months in than they are today, because of you You're the person the team wants on the ticket because they trust your judgement. What You Bring 3+ years in a technical support role within a SaaS or cloud-based company API fluency: you can read an API reference, reason about authentication, and say what a 401 rather than a 500 tells you about where the fault sits SQL you write yourself: given an unfamiliar schema you work out how the tables relate and write the join unaided Comfortable in logs, following a request across services and working backwards from an error Strong written communication, particularly to a customer who is unhappy Experience with customer support tools such as Zendesk, Intercom, Jira, Linear, others Startup-ready: adaptable, fast-moving, and hands-on We're not asking for production engineering experience or a computer science degree. We care what you can do, not how you got there. Location and other bits Based in our Chancery Lane office in London, Monday to Thursday, with Fridays from home Standard office hours Benefits include: on-site gym, private medical, pension and lunch provided everyday The Hiring Process Submit your CV (no need for a cover letter) We'll review it An initial call with someone from the hiring team to review your experience and motivation for joining (30 mins) A call with our Head of Customer Support on your experience and how you think technically (30 minutes) A live technical exercise (60 minutes) Meet more of the team (30 minutes) For the exercise we'll give you access to a small example application, a database, an API and its logs, a couple of days ahead, along with three customer tickets. You don't need to solve anything in advance, and you're welcome to use whatever AI tooling you normally would, because that's how the job actually works. We'll be paying attention to how you check its answers. Our Culture Our culture is intentional. It stems from the fact we're in the race of our lives to reshape one of the largest AI opportunities that exist; email. There is only first or last. We're going to win by: An obsession around the fact that every second counts, we have to move fast with intensity and drive hard every day. Never let it slide, be relentless in challenging yourself and others to strive for the best outcome. This culture is intense; it requires focus and discipline. So we'll do everything we can to remove distraction, support your wellbeing, and reward your impact Compensation: £65K – £75K • £65K – £75K Equity • £65K – £75K • £65K – £75K Equity Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full Time" ;
